## Roles & Access Control

* `WEBMASTER`: global admin, not part of firm; can generate invites, sync plans, view usage, cancel subscription override.
* `OPERATOR`: belongs to firm; manages leads/cases/notes/docs, booking windows/settings, billing page (initiate/cancel).

Public routes: intake + booking only.

---

## Core Entities (behavioral requirements)

### Lead

* fields: `firmId`, `leadType`, `payloadJson`, `payloadVersion`, `debtAmount` (numeric from dropdown), `status`, `createdAt`
* shown in operator UI as human-readable (render payload cleanly)

### Case

* created by lead conversion or manual
* minimum manual fields: name + email
* has `caseNumber` sequential per firm
* `CaseStatus`: `ACTIVE | CLOSED` (simplified for initial implementation)
* `caseType` is mutable over time
* stores `leadId?` reference AND **leadSnapshotJson** at conversion time

### Notes

* internal only; add-only; soft delete

### Documents

* operator-only upload
* allowed types: PDF/JPG/JPEG/PNG
* max 5MB per upload
* soft delete supported
* track per-doc `byteSize` + accounting for storage bytes (case + firm via rollups)

### Booking

* cannot exist without a lead
* timezone from firm
* availability = Google free/busy ∩ operator booking windows ∩ internal booked table
* public cannot self-cancel/reschedule

### Invites

* invite codes are email-bound, role-encoded, expire in 10 days, not revocable
* must log invite attempts (success/fail + mismatch reasons)
* email normalization: trim + lowercase (must be consistent everywhere)

### Billing

* plans synced from Stripe catalog into DB
* firm chooses 1 plan
* operator can cancel subscription
* webhooks verified + idempotent + audited

### Usage Daily Rollups

Track per firm per day:

* leads created, cases created, bookings created
* file uploads count, storage bytes
* active operators
* webhook failures
* emails sent (only if implemented)

